@* UserDetail.razor — Phase 6.3

   Staff-facing user detail page at route `/Admin/Users/{Id:guid}`. Reached
   from the /Admin/Users list page (Phase 6.1) by clicking the "View
   details" (visibility) icon in the actions column. Page-level gate is
   [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager")] — same as the list page — and the
   backend GetUserByIdQueryHandler additionally allows Employee to view
   (but not edit) any user. Customers/ReadOnly can only view their own
   profile via this same route (the handler enforces that defense-in-depth
   by returning a generic "not found" for other users).

   BACKEND CONTRACT:
     - Load: GetUserByIdQuery { UserId } → Result<UserDto>
       - Returns the UserDto (Id, WorkerId, FullName, Gender, GroupName?,
         IsActive, Email? [currently always null — TODO in handler], Roles list).
       - GroupName is only populated for Admin/Manager viewers; Employee
         viewers get null (handler defense-in-depth).
       - Returns Result.Failure("User '...' was not found.") for both
         genuinely-missing users AND viewers-not-allowed-to-see (the
         canonical "never leak existence" pattern, same as GetSaleByIdQuery).
     - Edit FullName: UpdateUserFullNameCommand(UserId, NewFullName) → Result
       - [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]. Validator: NewFullName non-empty,
         ≤ 200 chars.
     - Assign role: AssignUserRoleCommand(UserId, Role) → Result
       - [RequireRoles(Admin)]. Validator: Role must be one of
         {Admin, Manager, Employee, ReadOnly, Customer}.
     - Remove role: RemoveUserRoleCommand(UserId, Role) → Result
       - [RequireRoles(Admin)]. Handler rejects self-removal of own Admin
         role (defense-in-depth). Validator: same as Assign.
     - Assign to group: AssignUserToGroupCommand(UserId, GroupName) → Result
       - [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]. Validator: GroupName non-empty,
         ≤ 100 chars.
     - Remove from group: RemoveUserFromGroupCommand(UserId) → Result
       - [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]. Validator: UserId non-empty.

   LAYOUT (responsive — mirrors SaleDetail.razor's 12-col grid):
     Desktop / tablet (≥992px): two columns
       Left  (8/12): profile card + roles card + group card
       Right (4/12): sticky action panel (help + role-scope info + error)
     Mobile (<992px): single column, action panel collapses to top

   ROLE-RESOLUTION PATTERN:
     _isAdmin, _isManager, _currentUserId are computed in OnInitializedAsync
     via AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync() — NOT via
     ICurrentUserService.IsInRole (which returns false for everyone in
     interactive Blazor Server mode because HttpContext is null over the
     SignalR circuit). Same pattern as AdminUsers.razor (Phase 6.1) and
     SaleDetail.razor (Phase 4.3). See those files' header comments for
     the full rationale. The Wolverine command handlers ALSO enforce
     [RequireRoles] server-side as defense-in-depth.

   UX PATTERNS:
     - Edit FullName: opens a JS prompt() pre-filled with the current
       FullName. Same pattern as SaleDetail.razor's Cancel reason flow.
       Client-side validates 1-200 chars (matches validator) before
       dispatching; the validator also enforces this server-side.
     - Assign role: RadzenDropDown (TValue=string, primitive key — matches
       AdminUsers.razor's activity-filter pattern, NOT the complex-object
       binding pattern that bit us in CreateUser.razor Phase 6.2). Dropdown
       options are filtered to remove roles the user already has, AND to
       remove Customer (Customer is implicit — set at creation time, not
       assignable post-creation from this UI).
     - Remove role: small icon button per assigned role. Hidden on the
       current user's own Admin role (handler rejects this as
       defense-in-depth, but hiding the button is better UX — same pattern
       as AdminUsers.razor hiding self-Deactivate).
     - Assign to group: JS prompt() pre-filled with the current GroupName
       (or empty). Client-side validates 1-100 chars (matches validator).
     - Remove from group: direct button click (with a JS confirm() because
       it's destructive — removes the user's purchase-limit group).
     - All actions are wrapped in ExecuteActionAsync (mirrors SaleDetail)
       which: sets _isBusy, clears _actionError, dispatches, toasts on
       success/failure, reloads the user on success.

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Not needed — no EditForm. All button clicks are async event handlers
     that dispatch commands via Wolverine. The Blazor circuit's anti-forgery
     token is established at circuit start. (Same as SaleDetail.razor.) *@

@page "/Admin/Users/{Id:guid}"
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager")]
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Users.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Queries.GetUserById
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.UpdateUserFullName
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.AssignUserRole
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.RemoveUserRole
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.AssignUserToGroup
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.RemoveUserFromGroup
@using TakOne.Domain.Users
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<UserDetail> Loc
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthStateProvider
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<PageTitle>@(_user is null ? Loc["PageTitle"] : $"{_user.WorkerId} — {Loc["PageTitle"]}")</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            /* Layout — 12-col grid on desktop/tablet, stacks on mobile.
                           Left = profile + roles + group cards (wider); right = sticky action panel.
                           Mirrors SaleDetail.razor's .detail-grid structure. */
            .detail-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
                gap: 1.5rem;
                align-items: start;
            }

            @@media (max-width: 992px) {
                .detail-grid {
                    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
                    gap: 1rem;
                }
                    /* On mobile, action panel comes FIRST so help + role-scope
                                   context is visible before the user scrolls to the cards. */
                    .detail-grid .detail-action-panel {
                        order: -1;
                    }
            }

            /* Page header — worker ID (monospace) + active badge inline. */
            .detail-header {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 1rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

            .detail-worker-id {
                font-family: var(--rz-monospace-font-family, ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace);
                font-size: 1.6rem;
                font-weight: 700;
                margin: 0;
                line-height: 1.2;
            }

            /* Breadcrumb (same style as SaleDetail.razor). */
            .breadcrumb {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                font-size: 0.875rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
            }

                .breadcrumb a {
                    color: var(--rz-primary);
                    text-decoration: none;
                }

                    .breadcrumb a:hover {
                        text-decoration: underline;
                    }

            .crumb-sep {
                opacity: 0.6;
            }

            .crumb-current {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-weight: 500;
            }

            /* Scope badge (large) in the action panel header — same shape
                           as SaleDetail.razor's .status-badge-large. */
            .status-badge-large {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
                padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
                border-radius: 9999px;
                font-size: 1rem;
                font-weight: 600;
                min-width: 120px;
                justify-content: center;
            }

            /* Per-scope background colors (semantic):
                           - Admin   → primary  (highest privilege — visually distinct)
                           - Manager → info     (mid privilege)
                           - Viewer  → base     (read-only) */
            .scope-bg-admin {
                background: rgba(63, 81, 181, 0.18);
                color: #1a237e;
            }

            .scope-bg-manager {
                background: rgba(33, 150, 243, 0.18);
                color: #0d47a1;
            }

            .scope-bg-viewer {
                background: rgba(158, 158, 158, 0.18);
                color: #424242;
            }

            /* Sticky action panel on desktop. */
            @@media (min-width: 993px) {
                .detail-action-panel {
                    position: sticky;
                    top: 1rem;
                }
            }

            /* Profile card — 2-column field grid (label + value). */
            .profile-grid {
                display: grid;
                grid-template-columns: minmax(120px, 1fr) minmax(0, 2fr);
                gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
                align-items: baseline;
            }

            .profile-label {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 0.875rem;
                font-weight: 500;
            }

            .profile-value {
                font-weight: 500;
                word-break: break-word;
            }

            .profile-value-mono {
                font-family: var(--rz-monospace-font-family, ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace);
                font-weight: 600;
            }

            .profile-value-muted {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-style: italic;
            }

            /* Role badges list — horizontal flex wrap with remove buttons. */
            .role-list {
                display: flex;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                align-items: center;
            }

            .role-item {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.4rem;
            }

            .role-remove-btn {
                cursor: pointer;
                background: transparent;
                border: none;
                color: inherit;
                opacity: 0.7;
                padding: 0;
                line-height: 1;
                font-size: 1rem;
            }

                .role-remove-btn:hover {
                    opacity: 1;
                }

            .role-empty {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-style: italic;
            }

            /* Inline action forms — assign role / assign group rows. */
            .inline-form {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.5rem;
                align-items: stretch;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
                margin-top: 0.75rem;
            }

                .inline-form .rz-dropdown {
                    flex: 1 1 180px;
                    min-width: 160px;
                }

            /* Help panel bullets. */
            .help-list {
                margin: 0;
                padding-left: 1.25rem;
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-size: 0.875rem;
                line-height: 1.55;
            }

                .help-list li {
                    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
                }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Back button ──
       Returns to /Admin/Users. forceLoad:false preserves the Blazor circuit. *@
    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["BackToList"]"
                  Icon="arrow_back"
                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Light"
                  Variant="Variant.Text"
                  Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Users", forceLoad: false))" />

    @* ── Loading state ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenCard>
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
                <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Medium" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["Loading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Error state ── *@
    else if (_loadError is not null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                          Icon="refresh"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@LoadUserAsync"
                          Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
        </RadzenAlert>
    }

    @* ── Not found ──
       The handler returns Result.Failure with a "not found" message for
       both genuinely-missing users AND users the caller isn't allowed
       to see (defense-in-depth — never leak existence). Either way, the
       user sees the same friendly message. Same pattern as SaleDetail.razor. *@
    else if (_user is null)
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["NotFoundTitle"]"
                     Text="@Loc["NotFoundMessage"]"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Warning"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true" />
    }

    @* ── Main content ── *@
    else
    {
        <div class="detail-grid">
            @* LEFT — profile + roles + group cards *@
            <div>
                @* Breadcrumb: Manage users / [Worker ID] *@
                <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="breadcrumb" Style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                    <a href="/Admin/Users">@Loc["BreadcrumbUsers"]</a>
                    <span class="crumb-sep">/</span>
                    <span class="crumb-current">@_user.WorkerId</span>
                </nav>

                @* Page header — worker ID + active badge inline *@
                <div class="detail-header" Style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    <h1 class="detail-worker-id">@_user.WorkerId</h1>
                    @if (_user.IsActive)
                    {
                        <RadzenBadge Text="@Loc["StatusActive"]" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Success" IsPill="true" />
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <RadzenBadge Text="@Loc["StatusInactive"]" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Light" IsPill="true" />
                    }
                </div>

                @* ── Profile card ──
                   Read-only identity fields. FullName has an inline "Edit"
                   button that opens a JS prompt (handled in the right-side
                   action panel — here we just display the value). Group is
                   shown only when _canManageGroup (Admin/Manager) — the
                   handler already strips GroupName from Employee viewers. *@
                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    <RadzenText Text="@Loc["ProfileCardTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" Style="margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 600;" />

                    <div class="profile-grid">
                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColWorkerId"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value profile-value-mono">@_user.WorkerId</div>

                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColFullName"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value">
                            @_user.FullName
                            @if (_canEditFullName)
                            {
                                <RadzenButton Icon="edit"
                                              Text="@Loc["ActionEditFullName"]"
                                              Variant="Variant.Text"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Info"
                                              Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                              Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                              Click="@HandleEditFullNameAsync"
                                              Style="margin-left: 0.5rem;" />
                            }
                        </div>

                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColGender"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value">@GetGenderLabel(_user.Gender)</div>

                        <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColStatus"]</div>
                        <div class="profile-value">
                            @if (_user.IsActive)
                            {
                                <RadzenBadge Text="@Loc["StatusActive"]" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Success" IsPill="true" />
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <RadzenBadge Text="@Loc["StatusInactive"]" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Light" IsPill="true" />
                            }
                        </div>

                        @* Email is currently always null in the DTO (TODO
                           in handler — IUserAccountService has no GetEmailAsync
                           yet). When the handler is extended, this row will
                           light up automatically without UI changes. *@
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_user.Email))
                        {
                            <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColEmail"]</div>
                            <div class="profile-value profile-value-mono">@_user.Email</div>
                        }

                        @* Group row — only shown to Admin/Manager. The
                           handler strips GroupName for Employee viewers, so
                           showing an empty value would be misleading. We
                           hide the whole row when the viewer lacks permission. *@
                        @if (_canManageGroup)
                        {
                            <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColGroup"]</div>
                            <div class="profile-value">
                                @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_user.GroupName))
                                {
                                    <span class="profile-value-muted">@Loc["GroupNone"]</span>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <RadzenBadge Text="@_user.GroupName" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Base" IsPill="true" />
                                }
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>
                </RadzenCard>

                @* ── Roles card ──
                   Shows the user's currently-assigned ASP.NET Identity roles.
                   Admin viewers can remove roles (per-role Remove button) and
                   add new roles (dropdown + Assign button). The dropdown is
                   filtered to exclude already-assigned roles AND the Customer
                   role (Customer is implicit — set at creation time, not
                   assignable post-creation from this UI). The Remove button
                   is hidden on the current user's own Admin role (handler
                   rejects self-Admin-removal as defense-in-depth). *@
                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                    <RadzenText Text="@Loc["RolesCardTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" Style="margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 600;" />

                    @if (_user.Roles.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <div class="role-empty">@Loc["NoRoles"]</div>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="role-list">
                            @foreach (var role in _user.Roles)
                            {
                                <span class="role-item">
                                    <RadzenBadge Text="@GetRoleLabel(role)"
                                                 BadgeStyle="@GetRoleBadgeStyle(role)"
                                                 IsPill="true" />
                                    @if (_canManageRoles && !(_currentUserId == _user.Id && role == Roles.Admin))
                                    {
                                        <button type="button"
                                                class="role-remove-btn"
                                                title="@string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ActionRemoveRoleTitle"], GetRoleLabel(role))"
                                                aria-label="@string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ActionRemoveRoleTitle"], GetRoleLabel(role))"
                                                disabled="@_isBusy"
                                                @onclick="@(() => HandleRemoveRoleAsync(role))">
                                            <RadzenIcon Icon="close" />
                                        </button>
                                    }
                                </span>
                            }
                        </div>
                    }

                    @if (_canManageRoles)
                    {
                        <div class="inline-form">
                            <RadzenDropDown TValue="string"
                                            Data="@_assignableRoles"
                                            @bind-Value="_selectedRoleToAdd"
                                            Placeholder="@Loc["RoleSelectPlaceholder"]"
                                            Style="flex: 1 1 180px; min-width: 160px;" />
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionAssignRole"]"
                                          Icon="add"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                          Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                          Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                          Disabled="@(_isBusy || string.IsNullOrEmpty(_selectedRoleToAdd))"
                                          Click="@HandleAssignRoleAsync" />
                        </div>
                        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["RolesHelpText"]"
                                    TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["RolesManagerOnlyHint"]"
                                    TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
                    }
                </RadzenCard>

                @* ── Group card ──
                   Admin/Manager viewers can assign the user to a customer
                   group (sets User.GroupName via AssignUserToGroupCommand)
                   or remove them from their current group. Staff users have
                   null GroupName by domain design (User.CreateStaff doesn't
                   set one); customers may or may not have one. Removing a
                   user from their group affects their purchase limits, so
                   we use a JS confirm() before dispatching. *@
                @if (_canManageGroup)
                {
                    <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.25rem;">
                        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["GroupCardTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" Style="margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 600;" />

                        <div class="profile-grid">
                            <div class="profile-label">@Loc["ColCurrentGroup"]</div>
                            <div class="profile-value">
                                @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_user.GroupName))
                                {
                                    <span class="profile-value-muted">@Loc["GroupNone"]</span>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <RadzenBadge Text="@_user.GroupName" BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Base" IsPill="true" />
                                }
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="inline-form">
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionAssignGroup"]"
                                          Icon="group_add"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                          Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                          Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                          Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                          Click="@HandleAssignGroupAsync" />

                            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_user.GroupName))
                            {
                                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionRemoveGroup"]"
                                              Icon="group_remove"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                              Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                              Size="ButtonSize.Small"
                                              Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                              Click="@HandleRemoveGroupAsync" />
                            }
                        </div>
                        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["GroupHelpText"]"
                                    TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                    Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
                    </RadzenCard>
                }
            </div>

            @* RIGHT — sticky action panel: scope info + inline error + help *@
            <div class="detail-action-panel">
                <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1.25rem;">
                    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
                        @* Role-scope badge — at-a-glance who the viewer is. *@
                        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center;">
                            <span class="status-badge-large @GetScopeBadgeCssClass()">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="@GetScopeIcon()" />
                                @GetScopeLabel()
                            </span>
                        </div>

                        @* Manager-scope informational alert — explains
                           what Managers can vs cannot do on this page. *@
                        @if (!_isAdmin)
                        {
                            <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ManagerScopeTitle"]"
                                         Text="@Loc["ManagerScopeBody"]"
                                         AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Info"
                                         Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                         ShowIcon="true" />
                        }

                        @* Inline action error — populated by ExecuteActionAsync. *@
                        @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_actionError))
                        {
                            <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                                         Text="@_actionError"
                                         AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                                         Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                         ShowIcon="true" />
                        }

                        @* Quick action buttons — disabled while an action is in flight. *@
                        @if (_canEditFullName)
                        {
                            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ActionEditFullName"]"
                                          Icon="edit"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Info"
                                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                          Disabled="@_isBusy"
                                          Click="@HandleEditFullNameAsync"
                                          Style="width: 100%;" />
                        }

                        @* Help panel — explains what each action does. *@
                        <RadzenText Text="@Loc["HelpPanelTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" Style="font-weight: 600;" />
                        <ul class="help-list">
                            <li>@Loc["HelpPanel_EditFullName"]</li>
                            <li>@Loc["HelpPanel_AssignRole"]</li>
                            <li>@Loc["HelpPanel_RemoveRole"]</li>
                            <li>@Loc["HelpPanel_AssignGroup"]</li>
                            <li>@Loc["HelpPanel_RemoveGroup"]</li>
                        </ul>
                    </RadzenStack>
                </RadzenCard>
            </div>
        </div>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── Route parameter ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// User ID from the route (/Admin/Users/{Id:guid}). Bound by the Blazor
    /// router. Invalid Guid values trigger the router's NotFound template.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Guid Id { get; set; }

    // ── State ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private UserDto? _user;
    private string? _loadError;
    private bool _isLoading = true;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the current user is in the Admin role. Computed via
    /// AuthenticationStateProvider in OnInitializedAsync — NOT via
    /// ICurrentUserService.IsInRole (which returns false over the SignalR
    /// circuit because HttpContext is null). Gates role-management UI
    /// (Assign/Remove role buttons). The Wolverine handlers also enforce
    /// [RequireRoles(Admin)] server-side as defense-in-depth.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isAdmin;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the current user is in the Manager role. Combined with
    /// _isAdmin to gate FullName editing and group management UI (both
    /// commands have [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isManager;

    /// <summary>
    /// The current user's Domain User Id (from the "UserId" claim set by
    /// our custom IClaimsPrincipalFactory in Infrastructure). Used to hide
    /// self-Admin-removal (handler also rejects this, but hiding the button
    /// is better UX — same pattern as AdminUsers.razor hiding self-Deactivate).
    /// </summary>
    private Guid _currentUserId;

    /// <summary>
    /// True while any action (Edit FullName / Assign Role / Remove Role /
    /// Assign Group / Remove Group) is in flight. Disables ALL action
    /// buttons to prevent double-clicks.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isBusy;

    /// <summary>
    /// Inline error message for the action panel. Populated when an action
    /// fails (e.g. "User '...' was not found."). Cleared at the start of
    /// the next action by ExecuteActionAsync.
    /// </summary>
    private string _actionError = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// The role selected in the "Assign role" dropdown. Bound via
    /// @bind-Value (two-way) — RadzenDropDown with TValue=string (primitive
    /// key, matches AdminUsers.razor's activity-filter pattern, NOT the
    /// complex-object binding that bit us in CreateUser.razor Phase 6.2).
    /// Reset to null after a successful Assign.
    /// </summary>
    private string? _selectedRoleToAdd;

    /// <summary>
    /// The list of roles available for assignment. Computed in
    /// OnInitializedAsync and recomputed after each successful role
    /// Add/Remove (because the list excludes roles the user already has).
    /// Customer is intentionally excluded — Customer is implicit (set at
    /// creation time, not assignable post-creation from this UI).
    /// </summary>
    private List<RoleOption> _assignableRoles = new();

    /// <summary>
    /// All staff-role options (excludes Customer) used to build the
    /// assignable-roles list. The 4 staff roles match the AllowedStaffRoles
    /// set on CreateStaffCommandValidator.
    /// </summary>
    private static readonly string[] StaffRoles =
        { Roles.Admin, Roles.Manager, Roles.Employee, Roles.ReadOnly };

    private sealed class RoleOption
    {
        public string Value { get; init; } = string.Empty;
        public string Label { get; init; } = string.Empty;
    }

    // ── Derived permission flags ───────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the current user can edit FullName (matches
    /// UpdateUserFullNameCommand's [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _canEditFullName => _isAdmin || _isManager;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the current user can manage roles (matches
    /// AssignUserRoleCommand + RemoveUserRoleCommand's [RequireRoles(Admin)]).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _canManageRoles => _isAdmin;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the current user can manage group assignment (matches
    /// AssignUserToGroupCommand + RemoveUserFromGroupCommand's
    /// [RequireRoles(Manager, Admin)]).
    /// </summary>
    private bool _canManageGroup => _isAdmin || _isManager;

    // ── Lifecycle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Compute _isAdmin, _isManager, _currentUserId synchronously via
        // AuthStateProvider so the action-stack visibility doesn't flicker
        // on first render. NOTE: we deliberately do NOT use
        // ICurrentUserService.IsInRole here — in interactive Blazor Server
        // mode, ICurrentUserService resolves from IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext,
        // which is null over the SignalR circuit (only populated during the
        // initial prerender). The AuthStateProvider is the canonical source
        // for interactive components. The Wolverine command handlers also
        // enforce [RequireRoles] server-side (defense-in-depth).
        try
        {
            var authState = await AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync();
            var user = authState.User;

            if (user?.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true)
            {
                // The UserId claim is set by our custom IClaimsPrincipalFactory
                // in the Infrastructure layer — it's the Domain User's Guid Id.
                // Fallback to NameIdentifier for safety (same claim-resolution
                // pattern as AdminUsers.razor lines 522-523).
                var idClaim = user.FindFirst("UserId")?.Value
                              ?? user.FindFirst(System.Security.Claims.ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier)?.Value;
                if (Guid.TryParse(idClaim, out var parsedId))
                {
                    _currentUserId = parsedId;
                }

                _isAdmin = user.IsInRole(Roles.Admin);
                _isManager = user.IsInRole(Roles.Manager);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            // Non-fatal — _currentUserId stays Guid.Empty (no self-action
            // buttons hidden, which is safe but slightly worse UX) and
            // _isAdmin/_isManager stay false (all action UI hidden — safer
            // fallback if role resolution fails). The handler still enforces
            // [RequireRoles] server-side.
        }

        try
        {
            await LoadUserAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadUserAsync()
    {
        _isLoading = true;
        _loadError = null;

        try
        {
            var query = new GetUserByIdQuery { UserId = Id };
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<UserDto>>(query);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                _user = result.Value;
                RefreshAssignableRoles();
            }
            else
            {
                // result.Error contains the handler's user-friendly message.
                // For "not found" (covers both genuinely-missing AND
                // permission-denied), we show the same NotFound UI.
                _loadError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
                _user = null;
            }
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _loadError = Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
            _user = null;
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Rebuilds the assignable-roles list, excluding roles the user
    /// already has. Called after every successful Load (initial + reload
    /// after each action) so the dropdown never shows already-assigned
    /// roles. Customer is intentionally never in this list.
    /// </summary>
    private void RefreshAssignableRoles()
    {
        if (_user is null)
        {
            _assignableRoles = new();
            return;
        }

        _assignableRoles = StaffRoles
            .Where(r => !_user.Roles.Contains(r))
            .Select(r => new RoleOption { Value = r, Label = GetRoleLabel(r) })
            .ToList();

        // If the previously-selected role is no longer assignable (because
        // the user just got assigned it), clear the selection.
        if (_selectedRoleToAdd is not null
            && !_assignableRoles.Any(o => o.Value == _selectedRoleToAdd))
        {
            _selectedRoleToAdd = null;
        }
    }

    // ── Actions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Edit FullName via JS prompt() pre-filled with the current FullName.
    /// Client-side validates 1-200 chars (matches
    /// UpdateUserFullNameCommandValidator.MaxFullNameLength=200) before
    /// dispatching; the validator also enforces this server-side.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleEditFullNameAsync()
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !_canEditFullName) return;

        var input = await JS.InvokeAsync<string?>(
            "prompt",
            Loc["Prompt_NewFullName"],
            _user.FullName);

        // User clicked Cancel on the prompt, or entered empty/whitespace.
        // Silent abort — no error toast (the user explicitly chose not to
        // rename; we don't want to scold them).
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(input)) return;

        var newName = input.Trim();

        if (newName.Length > 200)
        {
            await Toast.Warning(Loc["FullNameLengthError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionEditFullName"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new UpdateUserFullNameCommand(_user.Id, newName)));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Assign the currently-selected role (_selectedRoleToAdd) to the user.
    /// The dropdown is filtered to exclude already-assigned roles, so this
    /// should always be a new role — but the handler/validator is the
    /// final authority server-side.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleAssignRoleAsync()
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !_canManageRoles) return;
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(_selectedRoleToAdd)) return;

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionAssignRole"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new AssignUserRoleCommand(_user.Id, _selectedRoleToAdd)));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Remove a specific role from the user. Hidden on the current user's
    /// own Admin role (handler rejects it as defense-in-depth — see
    /// RemoveUserRoleCommandHandler's self-removal guard — but hiding the
    /// button is better UX).
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleRemoveRoleAsync(string role)
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !_canManageRoles) return;
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(role)) return;

        // Belt-and-suspenders: the markup also hides this button, but the
        // check is cheap and the handler also rejects it. We don't want to
        // even attempt the dispatch.
        if (_currentUserId == _user.Id && role == Roles.Admin)
        {
            await Toast.Warning(Loc["CannotRemoveOwnAdminRole"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        // JS confirm() — role removal is reversible (re-assign) but worth
        // one click of friction so the admin doesn't accidentally lock
        // themselves or another user out of a feature.
        var confirmMessage = string.Format(
            CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
            Loc["ConfirmRemoveRole"],
            GetRoleLabel(role),
            _user.FullName);

        var confirmed = await JS.InvokeAsync<bool>("confirm", confirmMessage);
        if (!confirmed) return;

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionRemoveRole"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new RemoveUserRoleCommand(_user.Id, role)));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Assign the user to a customer group via JS prompt() pre-filled with
    /// the current GroupName (or empty). Client-side validates 1-100 chars
    /// (matches AssignUserToGroupCommandValidator.MaxGroupNameLength=100).
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleAssignGroupAsync()
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !_canManageGroup) return;

        var input = await JS.InvokeAsync<string?>(
            "prompt",
            Loc["Prompt_NewGroupName"],
            _user.GroupName ?? string.Empty);

        // Silent abort on Cancel / empty input.
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(input)) return;

        var groupName = input.Trim();

        if (groupName.Length > 100)
        {
            await Toast.Warning(Loc["GroupNameLengthError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionAssignGroup"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new AssignUserToGroupCommand(_user.Id, groupName)));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Remove the user from their current group. Uses JS confirm() because
    /// removing a customer from their group affects their purchase limits.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleRemoveGroupAsync()
    {
        if (_user is null || _isBusy || !_canManageGroup) return;
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_user.GroupName)) return;

        var confirmMessage = string.Format(
            CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
            Loc["ConfirmRemoveGroup"],
            _user.GroupName,
            _user.FullName);

        var confirmed = await JS.InvokeAsync<bool>("confirm", confirmMessage);
        if (!confirmed) return;

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionRemoveGroup"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new RemoveUserFromGroupCommand(_user.Id)));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Common wrapper for all 5 actions: sets _isBusy, clears the previous
    /// _actionError, dispatches the command, handles success (toast + reload
    /// the user to refresh roles/group/FullName) and failure (inline
    /// _actionError banner + error toast). Mirrors SaleDetail.razor's
    /// ExecuteActionAsync pattern exactly.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ExecuteActionAsync(string actionName, Func<Task<Result>> dispatch)
    {
        _isBusy = true;
        _actionError = string.Empty;

        try
        {
            var result = await dispatch();

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ActionSuccessFormat"], actionName),
                    summary: Loc["ActionSuccessTitle"]);

                // Reload the user to refresh the roles list, group badge,
                // and FullName display. Also rebuilds the assignable-roles
                // dropdown (excludes the just-assigned role, or restores
                // the just-removed role).
                await LoadUserAsync();
            }
            else
            {
                // result.Error contains the handler's user-friendly message
                // (e.g. "User '...' was not found.", or "You cannot remove
                // your own Admin role. Assign Admin to another user first.").
                _actionError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericAction"];
                await Toast.Error(_actionError, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _actionError = Loc["Error_GenericAction"];
            await Toast.Error(_actionError, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusy = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Display helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns the localized label for a Gender enum value. Same mapping
    /// as AdminUsers.razor's GetGenderLabel (Phase 6.1) — duplicated here
    /// so the detail page is self-contained without depending on
    /// AdminUsers.resx.
    /// </summary>
    private string GetGenderLabel(Gender gender) => gender switch
    {
        Gender.Male => Loc["GenderMale"],
        Gender.Female => Loc["GenderFemale"],
        _ => gender.ToString()
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns the localized label for a role constant. Falls back to the
    /// raw role name if no translation is defined. Same mapping as
    /// CreateUser.razor's role labels.
    /// </summary>
    private string GetRoleLabel(string role) => role switch
    {
        Roles.Admin => Loc["RoleAdmin"],
        Roles.Manager => Loc["RoleManager"],
        Roles.Employee => Loc["RoleEmployee"],
        Roles.ReadOnly => Loc["RoleReadOnly"],
        Roles.Customer => Loc["RoleCustomer"],
        _ => role
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// Maps a role to a Radzen BadgeStyle for color coding. Admin gets
    /// Danger (highest privilege — visually distinct). Manager gets
    /// Warning. Employee gets Info. ReadOnly gets Base. Customer gets
    /// Success (buyer role — positive connotation).
    /// </summary>
    private static BadgeStyle GetRoleBadgeStyle(string role) => role switch
    {
        Roles.Admin => BadgeStyle.Danger,
        Roles.Manager => BadgeStyle.Warning,
        Roles.Employee => BadgeStyle.Info,
        Roles.ReadOnly => BadgeStyle.Base,
        Roles.Customer => BadgeStyle.Success,
        _ => BadgeStyle.Base
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns the localized label for the current viewer's scope (shown
    /// in the action panel header).
    /// </summary>
    private string GetScopeLabel() => _isAdmin
        ? Loc["ScopeAdmin"]
        : _isManager
            ? Loc["ScopeManager"]
            : Loc["ScopeViewer"];

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns a Material icon name for the current viewer's scope.
    /// </summary>
    private static string GetScopeIcon() => "shield_person";

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns a CSS class for the scope badge. Admin = primary (highest
    /// privilege — visually distinct). Manager = info. Anything else =
    /// base (read-only viewer).
    /// </summary>
    private string GetScopeBadgeCssClass() => _isAdmin
        ? "scope-bg-admin"
        : _isManager
            ? "scope-bg-manager"
            : "scope-bg-viewer";
}